<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/google-adk/adk-20261012T231538/entity/0xe2ccd0d14145ca55-output> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model output" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"content\": \"Here's a thinking process:\\n\\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\\n   - User says: \\\"Lisbon is currently enjoying a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C with clear skies. As Portugal's capital, it sits on the Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n   - Then asks: \\\"Does the brief you are given mention the weather? Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n\\n2.  **Identify the Core Question:**\\n   - The user is asking whether \\\"the brief\\\" mentions the weather.\\n   - I need to check if the provided text (the \\\"brief\\\") mentions weather.\\n   - The text given: \\\"Lisbon is currently enjoying a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C with clear skies. As Portugal's capital, it sits on the Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n   - This text explicitly mentions weather: \\\"pleasant 21\\u00b0C with clear skies\\\".\\n\\n3.  **Determine the Response Format:**\\n   - The instruction says: \\\"Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n   - Since the brief does mention the weather, the answer should be PASS.\\n\\n4.  **Formulate Output:**\\n   - Just output \\\"PASS\\\" as requested. No extra text needed, but I'll make sure it's exactly \\\"PASS\\\" or \\\"FAIL\\\".\\n\\n   Check: The prompt says \\\"Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\" I'll output \\\"PASS\\\".\\n\\n   Wait, let me re-read carefully: \\\"Does the brief you are given mention the weather? Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n   The \\\"brief\\\" is the text provided: \\\"Lisbon is currently enjoying a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C with clear skies. As Portugal's capital, it sits on the Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n   Yes, it mentions weather (21\\u00b0C, clear skies).\\n   So PASS is correct.\\n\\n   I'll output just \\\"PASS\\\".\\u2705\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"content\": \"PASS\", \"type\": \"text\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/google-adk/adk-20261012T231538/step/0xe2ccd0d14145ca55> .

