    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"content\": \"We need to call weather_agent and facts_agent in parallel, then transfer to writer with the findings. The user wants a short brief on Lisbon's weather and facts. As coordinator, we need to call both agents in parallel. Then we will transfer to writer with the gathered info. Probably we need to pass combined request? The agents likely need a request string. We can call weather_agent with request: \\\"Lisbon weather\\\". facts_agent with request: \\\"Lisbon facts\\\". Then after we get responses, we need to transfer to writer. But the instruction: \\\"In your first reply, call every agent you need at once, in parallel. Then transfer to the writer with what they found.\\\" So we should first invoke both agents, then transfer to writer. However we cannot generate text other than the function call when transferring. But we need to transfer to writer with what they found. Probably we need to pass the gathered data to writer via transfer. But we need to first get the results. However we can call the agents and then in the same reply transfer? The instruction says \\\"In your first reply, call every agent you need at once, in parallel. Then transfer to the writer with what they found.\\\" Means we should output function calls for weather_agent and facts_agent, then after that maybe transfer. But we can't output text besides function calls. So we should output two function calls. Then after they return, we would transfer. But we are in the first reply; we can't wait for results. Possibly we need to call the agents, and then in the same reply also transfer to writer, but we don't have the data yet. Maybe we can pass a combined request that includes both? But the description: \\\"Then transfer to the writer with what they found.\\\" Might mean after we get the results, we transfer. But we need to produce something now. Probably we call both agents, then after they respond we will transfer. However the user expects a brief eventually. But guidelines: \\\"If you are the best to answer the question according to your description, you can answer it. If another agent is better ... transfer.\\\" We are coordinator, not writer. So we should transfer to writer after gathering data. So we need to call weather_agent and facts_agent now, then after we get results we will transfer. But we need to produce a reply that includes the function calls. So we will output two function calls.\\n\\nThus:\\n\\nCall weather_agent with request: \\\"Lisbon weather\\\".\\n\\nCall facts_agent with request: \\\"Lisbon facts\\\".\\n\\nWe'll output both.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"id\": \"call-70ffe441-b13a-4a9f-a71a-ed026758ce9f\", \"name\": \"weather_agent\", \"arguments\": {\"request\": \"Lisbon weather\"}, \"type\": \"tool_call\"}, {\"id\": \"call-dbdb4fb7-95c4-4921-b74a-ac52646c6861\", \"name\": \"facts_agent\", \"arguments\": {\"request\": \"Lisbon facts\"}, \"type\": \"tool_call\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]" ;
